[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3628687220","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-3628687220","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","id":3628687220,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YSV90","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T19:30:43Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T19:30:43Z","body":"> * Check order of operations (should FXAA be before or after tonemapping and/or glow)?\r\n\r\nI believe the order is the best it can be for the same reasons as described in my [earlier comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/89582#issuecomment-3259227525).\r\n\r\n> * Check if the luminance exposure multiplier is correctly applied. It's possible that I got it wrong, or that I'm doing the operation for no benefit.\r\n\r\nAt first glance, this looks right to me (I see that you've inverted it to match the style of the Compatibility renderer). I don't know FXAA well enough to know if there are implications to applying the luminance multiplier to `color` and all of the other samples after FXAA, which would obviously save quite a few multiplication operations.\r\n\r\nAlso, I notice that you're passing in `exposure`, but this is not used in `post.glsl`. I believe this is a bug(?) but I haven't looked too much into this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3628687220/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3633044248","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-3633044248","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","id":3633044248,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Yi9sY","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-09T16:04:43Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T16:04:43Z","body":"Additionally, all three copies of `do_fxaa` should probably be updated in this PR to remove some math; I'm not a shader compiler expert, but I don't see the harm in helping out the compiler a bit as follows:\r\n\r\nIn post.glsl:\r\n``` glsl\r\nfloat combined_luminance_multiplier = exposure / luminance_multiplier;\r\n```\r\nIn tonemap.glsl and tonemap_mobile.glsl:\r\n``` glsl\r\nfloat combined_luminance_multiplier = exposure * params.luminance_multiplier;\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd then in all three files, replace all `exposure * luminance_multiplier` with `combined_luminance_multiplier`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3633044248/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3633536135","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-3633536135","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","id":3633536135,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Yk1yH","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-09T17:56:43Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T17:56:43Z","body":"I've applied the changes/optimizations above and tested it on all renderers.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3633536135/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3633936366","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-3633936366","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","id":3633936366,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YmXfu","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-09T19:31:16Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T19:31:16Z","body":"> Also, I notice that you're passing in `exposure`, but this is not used in `post.glsl`. I believe this is a bug(?) but I haven't looked too much into this.\r\n\r\nI just tried a bit more with this: it seems that `exposure` is simply never applied with Environment Background Mode Canvas. Also, `exposure` is applied in earlier passes during 3D rendering in Compatibility, so in these cases it doesn't need to be a part of FXAA. It appears that there are a few things that need cleaning up before the use of `exposure` can make any sense in this new FXAA.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3633936366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3919513042","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-3919513042","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","id":3919513042,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pnwXS","user":{"login":"moonjank","id":258881824,"node_id":"U_kgDOD245IA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258881824?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank","html_url":"https://github.com/moonjank","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moonjank/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T08:55:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T08:55:21Z","body":"`EDGE_THRESHOLD_MIN,` `EDGE_THRESHOLD_MAX` and `SUBPIXEL_QUALITY` should be customizable. Not sure about `ITERATIONS.` [Here](https://gist.github.com/cart/7d2da58eb28c75c0952787f29f3e562f) is a customizable FXAA for those who want to customize these values. I believe customizable FXAA is especially important for compatibility due to not having many AA options.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3919513042/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3931020698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-3931020698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","id":3931020698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qTp2a","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T01:11:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T01:12:22Z","body":"Rebased and tested again, it works as expected. Thanks @allenwp for the feedback :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\n> I see that you've set `apply_color_adjustments_in_post` to `true`, but it does not seem to be active with 2D rendering, even when an Environment has been added with a background mode of Canvas\r\n> \r\n> [compat-fxaa.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24088687/compat-fxaa.zip)\r\n>\r\n> Is this intentional? (I haven't looked into whether this is normal for Godot or not, so maybe this makes sense?)\r\n\r\nThis is probably intentional. We generally don't want FXAA to apply to 2D rendering, as it'll make it look very blurry (small text becomes almost unreadable). SMAA doesn't hurt 2D rendering as badly, but it's still not ideal.\r\n\r\nPS: I can't download the project you linked (`Not Found`). It seems you're running into the same issue I was running into recently, where files uploaded can only be downloaded by the uploader.\r\n\r\n> `EDGE_THRESHOLD_MIN,` `EDGE_THRESHOLD_MAX` and `SUBPIXEL_QUALITY` should be customizable. Not sure about `ITERATIONS.` [Here](https://gist.github.com/cart/7d2da58eb28c75c0952787f29f3e562f) is a customizable FXAA for those who want to customize these values. I believe customizable FXAA is especially important for compatibility due to not having many AA options.\r\n\r\nBeing able to adjust FXAA (or SMAA) parameters should be discussed in its own [proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals). If it's implemented, it should also be done in Forward+ and Mobile.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3931020698/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176278113","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-4176278113","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","id":4176278113,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc747PJh","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T10:37:20Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T10:37:20Z","body":"Tested locally, it works as expected on desktop hardware \r\n(Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 63.91 GiB memory)\r\n\r\nTesting project:\r\n[new-game-project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26435035/new-game-project.zip)\r\n\r\nThe shader fails to compile on web (or any OpenGL ES 3 backend) with the following error:\r\n<img width=\"827\" height=\"248\" alt=\"error\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d00b55b0-d67b-44d5-a78e-31bff4376e88\" />\r\nIt looks like the compiler is complaining about the `QUALITY` function comparing ints to floats:\r\n```glsl\r\nfloat QUALITY(float q) {\r\n\treturn (q < 5 ? 1.0 : (q > 5 ? (q < 10 ? 2.0 : (q < 11 ? 4.0 : 8.0)) : 1.5));\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis next part isn't inherently related to this PR, just something I've noticed.\r\nWhen using a tonemapper with non-default settings, for instance:\r\n<img width=\"475\" height=\"140\" alt=\"tonemap\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/875e707e-5e44-40d0-ae49-edbbe04daf47\" />\r\nThe colors will become much less saturated when FXAA is enabled.\r\n\r\n| No FXAA | FXAA |\r\n|-----------|-------|\r\n| ![nofxaa](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c3770c5-c3c6-477b-9037-8fefa8cd3dc1) | ![wfxaa](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/672bba30-c482-42b1-b497-cd60bef6ed02) |\r\n\r\nI personally don't consider this a blocking issue, since the same effect happens on the master branch with SSAO enabled. Just something to keep in mind.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176278113/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5225989630","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-5225989630","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","id":5225989630,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN35F_g","user":{"login":"pyhfen","id":304356368,"node_id":"U_kgDOEiQcEA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/304356368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen","html_url":"https://github.com/pyhfen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-08T11:55:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-08T11:55:19Z","body":"FXAA doesnt work on aliasing caused by SSAO. MSAA doesnt do anything either.\r\n<img width=\"885\" height=\"489\" alt=\"compare\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/67136eea-2d7a-442a-93fb-9ba257ef4f45\" />\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5225989630/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]